      "writtenOn": "2024-01-10T23:20:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This sounded very reasonable to me. But as I started implementing it, it revealed an issue in my ToT implementation of `apex_contributions`. The ToT implementation uses a `sourceModuleName -\u003e selectedModuleName` mapping, and this inherently depends on a [naming convention](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/build/soong/+/606dc4ff5518654a118d9222ca5e405519723a4c:android/apex_contributions.go;l\u003d105;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d0;drc\u003dda739a30a6575ae0345e6694da6ff65b1eceabba). When we have multiple prebuilts, we cannot rely on this naming convention to construct the key of this map.\n\nGetting the key will require us to get a handle to the module. Since `all_apex_contributions` are at the bottom of the graph, it is not possible to do so.\n\nSo I think we do need a two pass approach, but for this different reason. I have also updated the apex_contributions and drop baseModuleName entirely from the provider.",
      "parentUuid": "8125374d_82a338b7",
      "revId": "5ecbac07e30115d4b59155cbcc34f38b041d96e4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
